+    Yields patches from image items read from an input dataset. The patches are chosen in a contiguous grid sampling
+    scheme by a patch generator, such as :py:class:`PatchIter`, and each patch is optionally post-processed by a
+    transform applied to the patch alone.
+
+    By default each element is a (patch, coordinates) pair, where the patch has shape (channel, *patch_size) and the
+    coordinates are an integer array of shape (channel + spatial dimensions, 2) whose row ``i`` is ``[start_i, stop_i]``
+    in the unpadded frame of the image. For example, for a dataset of two single-channel 4x4 images:
+
